Subject: [PATCH] wsi/metal: respect VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_OPAQUE_BIT_KHR on CAMetalLayer

Upstream Mesa forced CAMetalLayer.opaque = NO for non-software drivers
(KosmicKrisp) to work around a Metal 4 presentation bug. Leaving the
layer non-opaque prevents macOS Direct-to-Display scanout and forces
WindowServer to alpha-composite every frame (observed at 40-80% CPU).

Honor the swapchain's opaque_composition flag so fullscreen opaque
swapchains can use Direct-to-Display on macOS 26+.

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
@@ -893,13 +893,11 @@
    const bool immediate_mode =
       pCreateInfo->presentMode == VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR;
 
-   /* Non-software implementations need to work around a Metal bug
-    * when presenting through Metal4. This is accomplished through
-    * setting the layer's opaque value to false. And since we will
-    * be blitting to the drawable, which means rendering, we can
-    * set the framebuffer only usage.
+   /* Honor the requested composite alpha so opaque fullscreen swapchains
+    * can use macOS Direct-to-Display instead of forcing WindowServer to
+    * alpha-composite every frame.
     */
-   const bool layer_opaque = opaque_composition && wsi_device->sw;
+   const bool layer_opaque = opaque_composition;
    const bool framebuffer_only = !wsi_device->sw;
 
    VkResult result = wsi_metal_layer_configure(metal_surface->pLayer,
